        ":question/id": "00bc9b45-dbe4-5490-9350-bc28715ad92a",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-168113",
        ":question/problem": "The divergence $\\text{div}\\,V$ of the velocity field represents the scalar rate of expansion of the fluid per unit of area at a given point. Find the corresponding expansion rate at the point $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The required rate of expansion is $\\text{div}\\,V\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "If $V=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $V$ all exist, then the divergence of $V$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot V=\\text{div}\\,V=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,V & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy) \\\\  & =2xy+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,V$ at the point $(1,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,V\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)} & =2(1)(1)+2(1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
